      <h2 id="deodorant-vs-body-spray">Deodorant vs Body Spray – System-Level Differences</h2>
      <p>Although deodorants and body sprays often share similar aerosol packaging formats — the same aluminium or tinplate cans, similar valve and actuator hardware — they are engineered to meet fundamentally different functional objectives, and treating them as interchangeable is a common beginner mistake that leads to performance or compliance failures. Deodorants prioritise odour control mechanisms by targeting the odour-generation process at the source, while body sprays function as fragrance delivery vehicles designed for broad sensorial coverage. This distinction influences everything from spray rate to application zone to usage frequency, and consequently drives different formulation strategies, actuator selections, and regulatory classifications in some jurisdictions.</p>

